1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:03,016
Soleil and Friends

2
00:00:08,513 --> 00:00:12,923
Why are they jogging together all of a sudden? I thought they were on bad terms up until yesterday.

3
00:00:12,923 --> 00:00:15,756
Right? Her attitude changed too suddenly, it's pretty sus!

4
00:00:15,756 --> 00:00:17,015
There's nothing "sus" about it.

5
00:00:17,495 --> 00:00:18,102
Vera!

6
00:00:18,102 --> 00:00:19,004
When did you get here?

7
00:00:19,004 --> 00:00:23,007
A young woman who grew up like a delicate flower in a greenhouse meets a delinquent and falls in love with him.

8
00:00:23,007 --> 00:00:24,945
It's an overused cliche in the love comedy genre!

9
00:00:24,945 --> 00:00:28,385
(I don't want to get involved with a young lady who knows nothing about the ways of the world.)

10
00:00:28,385 --> 00:00:29,445
(But...!)

11
00:00:29,445 --> 00:00:34,126
And then the class president character is sure to be devastated after her lifelong friend is taken away by the new transfer student!

12
00:00:34,126 --> 00:00:35,262
Is that true?

13
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:38,706
No way. I haven't known Jun since I was an infant, and I'm not devastated at all.

14
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:42,909
Then... why are those two enjoying a jogging date early in the morning anyway?

15
00:00:42,909 --> 00:00:44,850
A date with Soleil?

16
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:46,792
Why would I do that?? Hahahaha!

17
00:00:46,792 --> 00:00:48,957
Then what were you two doing together?

18
00:00:48,957 --> 00:00:50,000
Special training.

19
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,117
Special training?

20
00:00:51,117 --> 00:00:54,307
Basic physical fitness is essential if we want to catch Night Griffon.

21
00:00:54,307 --> 00:00:55,770
Here's what I had in mind!

22
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:57,734
Here it comes. Jun's mission briefing...

23
00:00:57,734 --> 00:00:58,938
I don't wanna hear it.

24
00:00:58,938 --> 00:01:02,147
When the observer spots Night Griffon, she'll confirm his route.

25
00:01:02,147 --> 00:01:05,546
The target is flying south-southwest towards that building. It's up to you now! (FX-italic)

26
00:01:05,546 --> 00:01:08,516
Next, the capturer runs up the building he's heading towards, and-

27
00:01:08,516 --> 00:01:09,324
Blue Cop! Set Up!! (FX-italic)

28
00:01:09,324 --> 00:01:10,193
Hiyaaaa!! (FX-italic)

29
00:01:10,193 --> 00:01:11,217
CAAAAW!! (FX-italic)

30
00:01:11,217 --> 00:01:16,757
I call this one, Operation: Sky Body Press! The key part is how quickly I can get up to the roof.

31
00:01:16,757 --> 00:01:18,647
That's why you were training?

32
00:01:18,647 --> 00:01:21,515
Why do you have to take the stairs? We have elevators for that.

33
00:01:22,515 --> 00:01:26,717
Soleil said Night Griffon flies at supersonic speeds. Won't he fly past the building before you even reach the top?

34
00:01:26,717 --> 00:01:27,820
Supersonic speed??

35
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:31,057
And I'm pretty sure he would be flying higher than a skyscraper, too.

36
00:01:31,057 --> 00:01:33,078
H-higher??

37
00:01:33,078 --> 00:01:35,879
Our efforts were all for nothing...

38
00:01:35,879 --> 00:01:37,394
I don't even know where to start with you.

39
00:01:37,394 --> 00:01:40,418
Hey, Soleil? Didn't you find anything wrong with Jun's plan?

40
00:01:40,418 --> 00:01:42,723
I ceded operational control to Jun.

41
00:01:42,723 --> 00:01:43,575
Ah...

42
00:01:43,575 --> 00:01:47,436
Sigh. Just hang on a sec. I'll fetch us a guy who can help.

43
00:01:47,436 --> 00:01:48,908
A guy who can help?

44
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:54,472
What kind of person are we meeting that'd bring us all the way out here? We need to get back and set up a new plan.

45
00:01:54,472 --> 00:01:56,454
Tch. Just hang on!

46
00:01:58,656 --> 00:01:59,834
Is that plane...

47
00:01:59,834 --> 00:02:00,615
Oh!

48
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:05,816
Welcome, Fleta Z.

49
00:02:05,816 --> 00:02:09,092
I was completely taken by surprise. I never expected to get a call from Miss Vera.

50
00:02:09,092 --> 00:02:10,603
I'm the one who's surprised here!

51
00:02:10,603 --> 00:02:13,360
How were you able to come all the way out here? What about your VIP security job?

52
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:16,046
Well, someone even more important to me than a VIP called, so I had to come.

53
00:02:16,046 --> 00:02:17,925
Of course, I asked the client for their understanding.

54
00:02:17,925 --> 00:02:19,638
Okay, I guess...

55
00:02:19,638 --> 00:02:21,859
Hey, what's your relation to Vera?

56
00:02:21,859 --> 00:02:25,697
We're best friends. We even share information about interesting VIPs.

57
00:02:25,697 --> 00:02:27,848
So that's why you responded so fast.

58
00:02:27,848 --> 00:02:32,802
Of course, I still cherish the memory of the romantic flight we shared together, Ms. Anna. Don't you worry.

59
00:02:32,802 --> 00:02:33,741
You womanizer!

60
00:02:33,741 --> 00:02:36,413
Ouchie♡ Hahahaha... Oh! Excuse me.

61
00:02:36,913 --> 00:02:39,479
My apologies for the late greeting. My name is Fleta Z.

62
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:41,389
Hi. I'm Soleil.

63
00:02:41,389 --> 00:02:45,129
Nice to meet you. I've heard a lot about you. How about you and I go out sometime later and-

64
00:02:45,129 --> 00:02:46,009
Get away from her.

65
00:02:46,009 --> 00:02:47,002
- Back off!!
- Beat it!!

66
00:02:47,002 --> 00:02:48,366
Owwie♡

67
00:02:48,366 --> 00:02:51,745
He hasn't changed at all... So? How are you gonna help us?

68
00:02:51,745 --> 00:02:54,067
Ah, yes! I heard the whole story.

69
00:02:54,067 --> 00:02:57,792
Night Griffon, huh... Would you like to hear my idea first?

70
00:02:59,051 --> 00:03:03,469
If you can't fly but want to take down enemies flying overhead, you'll need to start with basic training!

71
00:03:03,569 --> 00:03:05,854
Hey, this is just stamina training!

72
00:03:05,854 --> 00:03:09,000
Bingo! It's about pushing your strength to the limit!

73
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,568
That means I was right all along.

74
00:03:10,568 --> 00:03:11,756
Yeah, congrats...

75
00:03:11,756 --> 00:03:14,611
Hey, hey, hey. Do I need to get even stronger? I'm already super strong, ya know!

76
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:17,389
Bzzzzt... But I can fly...

77
00:03:17,389 --> 00:03:18,449
Why am I doing this too?

78
00:03:18,449 --> 00:03:20,430
Because this is how you cooperate.

79
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:23,144
Next, we'll do a special training session to improve your sense of balance.

80
00:03:23,144 --> 00:03:24,569
Up we go...

81
00:03:27,577 --> 00:03:29,077
Will this training- (FX-jump)

82
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,700
-actually help us- (FX-jump)

83
00:03:30,838 --> 00:03:32,112
-c-capture him?? (FX-jump)

84
00:03:32,112 --> 00:03:36,778
Of course it will! Only those who can control their posture in the air can conquer the skies!

85
00:03:36,778 --> 00:03:39,387
Just like me, Ms. Cielo, and Lady Sky Gallop.

86
00:03:39,387 --> 00:03:40,207
I see. (FX-jumpdown)

87
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,100
Like this? (FX-jump jumpfast)

88
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,000
Ha! (FX-jump jumpfast)

89
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:43,409
Hoo! (FX-jump)

90
00:03:43,409 --> 00:03:45,173
You're doing great, Blue Cop!

91
00:03:45,173 --> 00:03:47,129
Excellent! Higher now!

92
00:03:48,129 --> 00:03:49,286
Hiya!

93
00:03:49,286 --> 00:03:49,860
Woah!! (FX-jumpdown)

94
00:03:51,677 --> 00:03:52,399
Ow...

95
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,340
I'm okay...

96
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:54,757
That's alright. Let's try again!

97
00:04:01,778 --> 00:04:05,317
Bzzzyawn... How much longer do we have to do this?

98
00:04:07,295 --> 00:04:09,735
We sure this kind of training is really gonna help us?

99
00:04:09,735 --> 00:04:12,606
One more time, please! This time, I'll succeed for sure!

100
00:04:12,606 --> 00:04:13,602
Easy for you to say.

101
00:04:13,602 --> 00:04:14,019
Huh?

102
00:04:14,019 --> 00:04:18,113
Have you ever considered how difficult it is for us down here to keep catching you when you fall?

103
00:04:18,113 --> 00:04:20,415
It's like you aren't even trying!

104
00:04:21,415 --> 00:04:22,843
What do you think you're doing?!

105
00:04:25,913 --> 00:04:27,925
We doin' this?! Huh?!

106
00:04:31,076 --> 00:04:31,576
Grr...

107
00:04:31,576 --> 00:04:32,444
Grrr!

108
00:04:32,444 --> 00:04:33,696
AWOOOO!!

109
00:04:36,447 --> 00:04:38,278
Guys. Stop this.

110
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,959
It's only been a day since you two reconciled!!

111
00:04:40,959 --> 00:04:42,803
Extra Extra! It’s total mayhem!

112
00:04:42,803 --> 00:04:45,685
Bzzt. Hooray. Fight some more.

113
00:04:45,685 --> 00:04:46,749
You should join in, too!

114
00:04:46,749 --> 00:04:47,803
Eh?!

115
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,879
Well, well!

116
00:04:58,605 --> 00:05:00,932
This party looks quite entertaining to me.

117
00:05:00,932 --> 00:05:03,261
Might I join in on the- uh, fun?

118
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,564
W-what's going on here?

119
00:05:05,564 --> 00:05:06,464
Ku ku ku ku...

120
00:05:06,464 --> 00:05:07,547
He he he he...

121
00:05:07,547 --> 00:05:09,793
Hehehehehehehe!

122
00:05:09,793 --> 00:05:11,769
You fell right into our trap, Night Griffon.

123
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:12,904
Trap?

124
00:05:12,904 --> 00:05:16,882
That's right! All of this was a trap to lure you out.

125
00:05:16,882 --> 00:05:17,630
You...!

126
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:20,790
So far, you've only shown up whenever we've been fighting each other.

127
00:05:20,889 --> 00:05:22,629
May I join in too? (FX-italic)

128
00:05:22,629 --> 00:05:25,290
I'd quite like to join the fun, if you wouldn't mind. (FX-italic)

129
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:27,543
Which means you love fights to the very core.

130
00:05:27,543 --> 00:05:30,454
Plus, you're the type who loves to butt in on everything. It's a pretty nasty habit-

131
00:05:30,454 --> 00:05:31,776
-Will you let go of me already!?

132
00:05:31,776 --> 00:05:35,382
These are the reasons why we predicted you would show up when we fought.

133
00:05:35,382 --> 00:05:37,495
That means everything you've been doing is all just-

134
00:05:37,495 --> 00:05:38,639
-Acting, of course!

135
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:40,529
Everyone's acting was really convincing.

136
00:05:40,529 --> 00:05:42,050
I was on the edge of my seat, though...

137
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,521
I was fighting for real.

138
00:05:43,521 --> 00:05:44,420
Hey!

139
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:48,507
So you all dared to think you could play tricks on me... How bold of you!

140
00:05:48,507 --> 00:05:50,016
Phantom Hornet. Set Up!

141
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:50,997
Nope!

142
00:05:52,461 --> 00:05:53,406
Sting Raid!

143
00:05:55,538 --> 00:05:57,918
I let my guard down last time, but that's not gonna happen again!

144
00:05:57,918 --> 00:05:59,119
Blue Cop! Tigun!

145
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:03,274
What’s going on, you lot?! Are you- of all bots- working as a team?!

146
00:06:03,274 --> 00:06:08,786
Even so, a single gnat and some beasts crawling along the ground are nothing but my playthings!

147
00:06:08,786 --> 00:06:10,970
You seem to have forgotten that I’m here, too.

148
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:12,358
Fleta Z! Set Up!

149
00:06:13,074 --> 00:06:14,180
Beak Arrow!

150
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:21,408
I never thought I’d see the Hunter of the Wilds here of all places. It’s a small world after all, "Brother".

151
00:06:21,408 --> 00:06:25,153
And I, for one, am delighted to see the Predator of Pitch Black once more!

152
00:06:30,095 --> 00:06:33,324
But it seems your skills have gotten a bit rusty while I was away.

153
00:06:33,324 --> 00:06:35,481
Heh, heh... I cannot deny that.

154
00:06:35,481 --> 00:06:39,250
I’ve been carried away having too much fun because of my new friends here, including a few fair ladies!

155
00:06:40,250 --> 00:06:41,730
Now, Phantom Hornet!

156
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:46,086
Give me back my lovely Crimson Lance!!

157
00:06:46,086 --> 00:06:49,648
Nuh-uh! This town ain't big enough for the two of us stingers!

158
00:06:51,646 --> 00:06:52,415
They're coming this way!

159
00:06:52,415 --> 00:06:55,276
Perfect. Fleta Z, come back here! Tigun! Get ready!

160
00:06:56,634 --> 00:06:57,093
Bzzz...

161
00:06:57,093 --> 00:07:00,680
Haha! You cannot escape me with those puny wings of yours!

162
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,889
Bzzzt! Soleil! Now!

163
00:07:02,889 --> 00:07:04,288
Alright! Now, Jun!

164
00:07:04,288 --> 00:07:05,059
Tigun!!

165
00:07:05,059 --> 00:07:07,095
Tiger!! Cannonade!!

166
00:07:07,095 --> 00:07:08,350
Here! You can have it!

167
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:08,983
Hm?

168
00:07:10,019 --> 00:07:11,509
CAAAWWWWWW!!!

169
00:07:15,434 --> 00:07:16,699
Don't let him escape, Blaion!

170
00:07:16,899 --> 00:07:18,281
Leon Roar Shot!!

171
00:07:19,281 --> 00:07:21,430
CAW!!

172
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:22,625
Nice shot!

173
00:07:22,625 --> 00:07:24,701
He won't be able to speed up anymore!

174
00:07:24,701 --> 00:07:26,423
Great job, you guys!

175
00:07:26,423 --> 00:07:28,519
Our plan worked, Soleil!

176
00:07:28,519 --> 00:07:29,814
I... yes.

177
00:07:31,195 --> 00:07:32,326
Those accursed fiends...

178
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:38,058
If you’re so eager to drag me down from heaven, I’ll come down myself, just as you wish!

179
00:07:38,058 --> 00:07:40,302
That technique...! We need to get out of here now!

180
00:07:40,302 --> 00:07:40,770
What?

181
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:42,350
He's nuthin' but a mere crow!

182
00:07:42,350 --> 00:07:45,054
Shout Of Beak!!

183
00:07:45,054 --> 00:07:46,370
Everyone! Clear the area!

184
00:07:47,370 --> 00:07:48,664
Soleil! What are you doing?!

185
00:07:48,664 --> 00:07:50,506
Give me your order, Soleil!

186
00:07:50,506 --> 00:07:52,043
We gotta go now!

187
00:07:52,043 --> 00:07:53,962
...Let's get out of here, Blaion!

188
00:07:54,263 --> 00:07:55,182
Tigun!

189
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:05,111
Jun probably thinks of you as a dear friend, too. That's why... (FX-italic soleilThink rhea)

190
00:08:05,111 --> 00:08:06,800
Are you saying that he thinks I'm the same as the likes of those Metal Cardbots?! (FX-italic soleilThink)

191
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,652
Are you saying that he thinks I'm the same as the likes of those Metal Cardbots?! (FX-italic)

192
00:08:08,958 --> 00:08:12,523
Soleil. Soleil! Wake up!

193
00:08:12,523 --> 00:08:13,774
Soleil!

194
00:08:14,917 --> 00:08:16,328
Soleil! Are you okay?

195
00:08:16,328 --> 00:08:17,471
Jun! Watch out!

196
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:23,788
(For machines from beyond the cosmos and humans to coexist, they must each respect the other’s boundaries.)

197
00:08:23,788 --> 00:08:31,049
(Machines must obey human commands, and humans must oversee the machines. Otherwise, humans would fall victim to the machines.)

198
00:08:31,049 --> 00:08:37,644
(I thought Jun, a master of the Metal Breath, understood that dynamic and merely referred to them as friends.)

199
00:08:37,644 --> 00:08:39,097
(But to Jun...)

200
00:08:39,097 --> 00:08:47,350
(To Jun, they’re all precious, genuine friends with whom he shares a close bond. Humans, Metal Cardbots, and Wild Cardbots... all of them.)

201
00:08:47,350 --> 00:08:49,100
And you... You're also my...

202
00:08:51,927 --> 00:08:55,957
Ho ho! There you are! I’ve been looking for you!

203
00:08:55,957 --> 00:08:58,534
Blaion...! Omega Heat Flame!

204
00:08:58,835 --> 00:09:01,769
Hm! Omega Heat Flame!!

205
00:09:03,143 --> 00:09:06,067
Let's go, Jun. Let's show him the results of our special training!

206
00:09:06,067 --> 00:09:09,232
Oh... Alrighty, Soleil! Let's do this, Blue Cop!

207
00:09:09,232 --> 00:09:11,634
Right! Blaion, Tigun, let's go!

208
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:12,446
We're doing the thing?

209
00:09:12,446 --> 00:09:13,820
Time for the real deal!

210
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,028
You pathetic ground dwellers!

211
00:09:16,028 --> 00:09:17,606
Phantom Hornet! Phantom Legion!

212
00:09:17,606 --> 00:09:18,308
Bzzt!!

213
00:09:27,456 --> 00:09:28,826
Go knock that guy out!

214
00:09:29,813 --> 00:09:31,201
Here we go!

215
00:09:31,201 --> 00:09:33,136
You little gnat- eh?

216
00:09:34,639 --> 00:09:35,451
Oh.

217
00:09:35,451 --> 00:09:36,033
Ah.

218
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:36,967
Eh?

219
00:09:41,188 --> 00:09:42,888
Alpha Thunder-

220
00:09:42,888 --> 00:09:43,679
Gh?!

221
00:09:43,679 --> 00:09:44,543
-Punch!!

222
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:46,494
CAAAAAAAW!!!

223
00:09:46,494 --> 00:09:49,232
Blue Cop floated like a butterfly, and stung like a bee!

224
00:09:49,232 --> 00:09:50,741
Fleta Z's special training!

225
00:09:50,741 --> 00:09:52,256
It wasn't in vain!

226
00:09:52,256 --> 00:09:54,265
As your teacher, I'm so proud of you, Blue Cop!

227
00:09:54,265 --> 00:09:55,751
We gon' finish him good!

228
00:09:55,751 --> 00:09:56,910
Leave it to us!

229
00:09:56,910 --> 00:09:58,510
Counting on youuuuu! (FX-fallshrink)

230
00:10:00,534 --> 00:10:02,518
Screech Of Prey!!

231
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:03,389
Time to end this!

232
00:10:03,389 --> 00:10:03,868
Yes!

233
00:10:03,868 --> 00:10:06,408
Growl Axe Tooth!

234
00:10:06,408 --> 00:10:09,332
Growl! Axe Tooth!!

235
00:10:09,332 --> 00:10:11,134
Infernal Stinger!

236
00:10:11,134 --> 00:10:13,227
Infernal Stinger!!

237
00:10:23,778 --> 00:10:26,463
That wasn't... half bad...

238
00:10:28,283 --> 00:10:29,663
How'd ya like that?

239
00:10:29,663 --> 00:10:30,980
Go ahead and seal him.

240
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:32,746
Uh... You sure?

241
00:10:32,746 --> 00:10:33,342
Yes.

242
00:10:33,926 --> 00:10:34,585
Okay!

243
00:10:35,719 --> 00:10:37,671
Wild Cardbot! Change Up!

244
00:10:47,788 --> 00:10:50,075
Night Griffon! Sealed!

245
00:10:51,203 --> 00:10:52,659
We did it!

246
00:10:52,659 --> 00:10:54,282
Yeah. We did.

247
00:10:54,282 --> 00:10:55,082
Uh...

248
00:10:55,082 --> 00:10:56,554
Clap his hand.

249
00:10:58,709 --> 00:11:00,931
This is why I've been telling you to work with us all along!

250
00:11:00,931 --> 00:11:03,337
Yes... I'll be counting on you from now on, Jun.

251
00:11:04,791 --> 00:11:08,421
Really? Another Wild Cardbot? Great job.

252
00:11:08,421 --> 00:11:10,147
So? Who sealed him?

253
00:11:10,147 --> 00:11:14,385
I'm sorry, Mother. Jun sealed Night Griffon.

254
00:11:14,385 --> 00:11:19,437
Yes, I'll make sure to seal the next one. I'll share the details later.

255
00:11:19,725 --> 00:11:22,558
You let your target get away, yet you seem relieved.

256
00:11:22,558 --> 00:11:23,463
I can't be relieved?

257
00:11:23,463 --> 00:11:26,298
You can. I'm fine with it if you're fine with it.

258
00:11:26,298 --> 00:11:28,038
I finally understood.

259
00:11:28,038 --> 00:11:29,217
About what?

260
00:11:29,217 --> 00:11:32,423
This is what we call a true friendship... Right?

